Run this in CMD inside your venv:

cmd
python -c "import pyodbc; print(pyodbc.drivers())"
This will output something like:

Code
['SQL Server', 'ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server', 'ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server']
If you do not see:

Code
ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server
then your SQL Server connection string must use a driver that does exist.

For example, if you see:

Code
SQL Server
then use:

python
DRIVER={SQL Server}
✅ 2. How to list ALL OLE DB providers installed (Oracle)
ADOX.Catalog does not work on many systems.

Use this instead — it works everywhere:

✔ Working provider enumeration script
python
import win32com.client

enum = win32com.client.Dispatch("ADO.ProviderEnum.1")
providers = enum.GetAll()

for p in providers:
    print(p)
Run:

Code
python ces_prov.py
This will print something like:

Code
MSDAORA
OraOLEDB.Oracle
SQLOLEDB
MSOLEDBSQL
If you do not see:

Code
MSDAORA
OraOLEDB.Oracle
then Oracle client is NOT installed, even if Oracle DB is on the same machine.
